---
import DocsLayout from '~/layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout slug="clients/action" title="GitHub Action" description="kotoshu/action-kotoshu@v1 — spell-check files in CI, cache dictionaries between runs, and upload SARIF to the Security tab.">
  <p class="docs-lead">
    One step, no credentials. The Action installs the gem, pre-warms the languages you name,
    checks the files you glob, and uploads SARIF to the Security tab.
  </p>

  <h2 class="display text-2xl mt-12">Quick start</h2>
  <pre class="code-block overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-7 mt-4"><code>jobs:
  spell-check:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      security-events: write   # for the SARIF upload
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: kotoshu/action-kotoshu@v1
        with:
          files: "*.md docs/**/*.adoc"
          language: en</code></pre>
  <p class="text-[15px] leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)] mt-4">
    Dictionaries are cached between runs under the default cache key; results land as code
    annotations and a SARIF report in the repository Security tab, plus a workflow artifact.
  </p>

  <h2 class="display text-2xl mt-12">Inputs</h2>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto mt-4"><table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead>
      <tr class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-text-3)]">
        <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-left">Input</th>
        <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-left">Default</th>
        <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-left">Purpose</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="px-3 py-2.5"><code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">files</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">.</td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">files or glob patterns, space-separated</td></tr>
      <tr class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="px-3 py-2.5"><code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">language</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">auto</td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">en, de, es, fr, pt, ru — or <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">auto</code> to detect per file</td></tr>
      <tr class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="px-3 py-2.5"><code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">format</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">sarif</td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">text, json, or sarif</td></tr>
      <tr class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="px-3 py-2.5"><code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">fail_on_error</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">true</td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">fail the step when errors are found</td></tr>
      <tr class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="px-3 py-2.5"><code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">version</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">latest</td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">pin the kotoshu gem version to install</td></tr>
      <tr class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="px-3 py-2.5"><code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">prewarm_languages</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">en</td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">languages to set up before the check</td></tr>
      <tr class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="px-3 py-2.5"><code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">offline</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">true</td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">skip the network — cached dictionaries only</td></tr>
      <tr class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="px-3 py-2.5"><code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">output_path</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">kotoshu-results.sarif</td><td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">where the SARIF/JSON report is written</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="text-[15px] leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)] mt-4">
    Outputs: <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">sarif-path</code> and
    <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">error-count</code>, for wiring into later steps.
    With <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">offline: true</code> the step still
    pre-warms with downloads allowed during the warm phase, then checks purely from cache — the
    pre-warm pattern from <a href="/docs/caching" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Caching &amp; resources</a>,
    already assembled.
  </p>

  <p class="dict-anno mt-10 border-t border-[var(--color-border-subtle)] pt-5">
    Validated 2026-09-05 — the workflow YAML above parses cleanly and its inputs match
    action-kotoshu v1's action.yml field for field; a full run against a test repository was judged
    overkill. <a href="https://github.com/kotoshu/action-kotoshu" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">action-kotoshu repo</a> ·
    <a href="https://github.com/kotoshu/action-kotoshu/blob/main/action.yml" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">action.yml</a>
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
